    "Genre: it is a reflective essay on a mental disorder; Acharya Ramchandra Shukla laid the foundation of this tradition with his essays on mental states in 'Chintamani', and Dinkar carried the tradition forward.",
    "Meaning of the title: 'Tu na gayi mere man se' (you never left my mind) — addressed to jealousy; it is an honest confession of human weakness, admitting that becoming fully free of jealousy is difficult.",
