     "Give a brief life-sketch of Karpoori Thakur.",
     "Karpoori Thakur was born on 24 January 1924 in a poor Nai family at Pitaunjhia village (now Karpoori Gram) in Samastipur district, Bihar. Father Gokul Thakur, mother Ramdulari Devi. He spent 26 months in jail for the 1942 Quit India Movement. After Independence he became a teacher; in 1952 he was first elected MLA from Tajpur. He became Bihar's first non-Congress socialist Chief Minister (1970) and served again in 1977–79. He passed away on 17 February 1988. In 2024 he was honoured posthumously with the Bharat Ratna.",
